ory. Each employee generates $47K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $42K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Workiva Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $3.8B market cap on $885M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years and +20% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Gross margins of 74% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $138M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.9%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 91% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9101472422803477},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 18.0% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (WK) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/81/Understanding_the_Setup:_WK_and_Scalable_Risk_112426072202_1795522922.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795522922.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can Workiva (NYSE:WK) Keep Its Competitive Advantage Intact Today?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/smallcap/can-workiva-nysewk-keep-its-competitive-advantage-intact-today","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795213140.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Is Workiva (NYSE:WK) Gaining Attention After Its Latest Update?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/technology/why-is-workiva-nysewk-gaining-attention-after-its-latest-update","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795033680.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.715,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(WK) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/34/WK_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets